1
00:00:02,002 --> 00:00:03,179
GORDON: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,203 --> 00:00:05,523
PENGUIN: <i>You paid off the
mayor to make Jim Gordon captain.</i>

3
00:00:06,139 --> 00:00:08,370
- Don't ever betray me again.
- Never.

4
00:00:08,475 --> 00:00:11,673
I need to know what Sofia is
planning and who she is planning it with.

5
00:00:12,045 --> 00:00:13,809
<i>Plain, dumb, Ed.</i>

6
00:00:13,881 --> 00:00:15,543
I would like you to
go to The Narrows

7
00:00:15,649 --> 00:00:17,379
and bundle him up and
bring him back to me.

8
00:00:17,651 --> 00:00:19,347
They're the ones
that are the problem.

9
00:00:19,686 --> 00:00:21,211
They work for Penguin.

10
00:00:22,422 --> 00:00:25,915
I would like to announce that
we just quit working for Penguin.

11
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:27,085
This is your turf now.

12
00:00:28,262 --> 00:00:29,372
SOFIA: <i>What is he doing to them?</i>

13
00:00:29,396 --> 00:00:30,557
GORDON: <i>He 's cooking them.</i>

14
00:00:30,664 --> 00:00:31,859
<i>They're people pies.</i>

15
00:00:32,132 --> 00:00:34,067
Eat the pies or the boy dies.

16
00:00:37,404 --> 00:00:38,531
SOFIA: <i>No!</i>

17
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:40,799
<i>Jim!</i>

18
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:48,606
GORDON: <i>The suspect
known as the Pyg is in custody.</i>

19
00:00:48,949 --> 00:00:50,508
<i>The GCPD kept its promise.</i>

20
00:00:51,184 --> 00:00:52,379
I'm not your enemy, Jim.

21
00:00:52,452 --> 00:00:53,681
I never will be.

22
00:00:55,589 --> 00:00:56,829
MAN: <i>Did you find anything out?</i>

23
00:00:59,693 --> 00:01:01,719
She will answer
for what she's done.

24
00:01:07,601 --> 00:01:10,002
(DISTORTED MUSIC
PLAYING ON PHONOGRAPH)

25
00:01:10,871 --> 00:01:11,871
PRISONER: Thursday.

26
00:01:12,406 --> 00:01:14,375
Thursday's my day.

27
00:01:14,841 --> 00:01:16,537
Thursday's my day.

28
00:01:16,643 --> 00:01:17,941
(PRISONER CONTINUES CHATTERING)

29
00:01:20,581 --> 00:01:21,913
Thursday's my day.

30
00:01:23,450 --> 00:01:24,450
(MUSIC STOPS)

31
00:01:32,426 --> 00:01:34,258
(OPERATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

32
00:01:56,683 --> 00:01:58,618
I don't like that song.

33
00:02:00,654 --> 00:02:02,418
My ma used to beat me to it.

34
00:02:03,323 --> 00:02:05,292
It was playing
when I killed her.

35
00:02:05,926 --> 00:02:06,926
(CHUCKLES)

36
00:02:08,495 --> 00:02:10,259
So now you turn it off.

37
00:02:11,465 --> 00:02:13,127
Or I do the same to you.

38
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:16,295
Why did your mother beat you?

39
00:02:19,106 --> 00:02:20,836
Were you a naughty boy?

40
00:02:22,676 --> 00:02:24,668
Did you soil your trousers?

41
00:02:27,447 --> 00:02:29,313
(MOCKS STUTTERING)

42
00:02:29,383 --> 00:02:30,383
Stutter,

43
00:02:31,318 --> 00:02:32,547
perhaps?

44
00:02:35,689 --> 00:02:36,748
- (GRUNTS)
- (GROANS)

45
00:02:38,358 --> 00:02:40,293
Open the gate.
Open the gate, now.

46
00:02:41,828 --> 00:02:43,660
All right, everybody calm down.

47
00:02:43,864 --> 00:02:45,332
(GUARDS CHATTERING)

48
00:02:47,334 --> 00:02:48,859
GUARD: Back off, just back off.

49
00:02:50,303 --> 00:02:52,465
I really wish you
hadn't done that.

50
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:01,341
(GROANS)

51
00:03:01,982 --> 00:03:04,315
I paid a fortune
to look this good.

52
00:03:05,252 --> 00:03:06,276
(YELLING)

53
00:03:07,287 --> 00:03:08,448
(LAUGHING)

54
00:03:09,222 --> 00:03:10,850
- (GROANING)
- (OPERATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

55
00:03:20,067 --> 00:03:21,365
(ALARM RINGING)

56
00:03:21,535 --> 00:03:22,535
(GUARDS SHOUTING)

57
00:03:23,403 --> 00:03:25,702
GUARD: Everybody,
stay where you are.

58
00:03:25,772 --> 00:03:27,400
All right, open the
gate, that's enough.

59
00:03:27,507 --> 00:03:30,238
Okay, it's over. Just
open the gate and let us in.

60
00:03:47,894 --> 00:03:50,363
LUCIUS: The doctors at
Arkham took these after the fight.

61
00:03:50,831 --> 00:03:51,911
The Pyg had titanium plates

62
00:03:51,998 --> 00:03:53,899
surgically grafted onto
the bones of his face,

63
00:03:53,967 --> 00:03:56,903
the result of which, radically
changed his appearance.

64
00:03:57,370 --> 00:03:59,566
When we booked him, his
fingerprints were burned off.

65
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:02,340
I've seen it before on criminals
that want to hide their identity.

66
00:04:02,809 --> 00:04:03,970
But never anything like this.

67
00:04:04,077 --> 00:04:06,137
That's not all. The doctors
also noticed scar tissue

68
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:07,908
behind his ears and
along his neckline,

69
00:04:08,014 --> 00:04:09,846
indicating he's had
multiple surgeries.

70
00:04:10,217 --> 00:04:12,243
That explains why we
couldn't ID him off his photo.

71
00:04:12,853 --> 00:04:14,048
This doesn't make any sense.

72
00:04:14,187 --> 00:04:15,553
The Pyg is a glory hound.

73
00:04:15,622 --> 00:04:18,217
Everything he's done, it's all
been about grabbing the spotlight.

74
00:04:18,291 --> 00:04:19,725
Classic sociopath behavior.

75
00:04:19,793 --> 00:04:21,887
So why doesn't he want
us to know who he really is?

76
00:04:22,462 --> 00:04:24,829
Now is the time he should
be taking credit for his crimes.

77
00:04:26,299 --> 00:04:28,791
Can you use this x-ray
to reconstruct his face?

78
00:04:29,336 --> 00:04:31,430
See what he looked like
before he had any work done?

79
00:04:31,805 --> 00:04:34,070
It's certainly possible,
but it'll take some time.

80
00:04:34,307 --> 00:04:35,400
Get started.

81
00:04:35,942 --> 00:04:37,740
I wanna know who
the Pyg really is.

82
00:04:41,882 --> 00:04:44,078
- Morning, Cap.
- Harper.

83
00:04:44,751 --> 00:04:45,878
How's the shoulder?

84
00:04:45,952 --> 00:04:47,580
This? Just a scratch.

85
00:04:48,088 --> 00:04:49,147
You got a visitor.

86
00:04:53,393 --> 00:04:54,417
Thanks.

87
00:04:57,597 --> 00:05:00,499
Sofia, what are you doing here?

88
00:05:01,768 --> 00:05:03,464
I haven't heard from
you in a few days.

89
00:05:04,137 --> 00:05:05,935
I didn't realize I
was supposed to call.

90
00:05:07,774 --> 00:05:09,504
I figured after the other night,

91
00:05:09,609 --> 00:05:11,475
we were gonna start
seeing each other again.

92
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:13,979
We're not.

93
00:05:15,482 --> 00:05:16,609
I get it.

94
00:05:16,683 --> 00:05:18,628
You're worried about
Penguin finding out about us,

95
00:05:18,652 --> 00:05:20,314
that I made you Captain.

96
00:05:21,021 --> 00:05:22,080
You don't have to be.

97
00:05:22,155 --> 00:05:23,350
I already told him.

98
00:05:24,591 --> 00:05:26,219
I'm sorry, you did what?

99
00:05:26,326 --> 00:05:27,624
I have it under control.

100
00:05:27,694 --> 00:05:28,855
Is that what you think?

101
00:05:29,696 --> 00:05:30,959
It's what I know.

102
00:05:31,364 --> 00:05:34,198
I am going to remove
Penguin from the picture,

103
00:05:34,534 --> 00:05:37,231
and when I do, I
want us to be together.

104
00:05:39,306 --> 00:05:41,070
It's not gonna work, Sofia.

105
00:05:41,174 --> 00:05:43,609
Even if Penguin
is out of the picture.

106
00:05:43,844 --> 00:05:46,370
I just don't see a way
forward for us. I'm sorry.

107
00:05:52,319 --> 00:05:53,844
(PEOPLE ARGUING)

108
00:05:56,690 --> 00:05:59,353
WOMAN: I run the dog
races, he runs the cock fights.

109
00:05:59,526 --> 00:06:01,586
Now he's coming and
muscling in on my business.

110
00:06:01,695 --> 00:06:04,392
- I got mouths to feed.
- You race those dogs again

111
00:06:04,564 --> 00:06:06,055
and I'll slit your damn throat.

112
00:06:06,166 --> 00:06:08,192
All right. Enough.

113
00:06:08,568 --> 00:06:10,503
If she stabs him,
it solves the issue.

114
00:06:10,904 --> 00:06:14,705
I started this court, so we could
work out disputes peacefully.

115
00:06:14,908 --> 00:06:18,072
This is how things are gonna be
done from now on, understood?

116
00:06:18,845 --> 00:06:20,837
Now you're both admitting
to having down months.

117
00:06:20,914 --> 00:06:23,042
Seems the only solution
is for you to partner up.

118
00:06:24,251 --> 00:06:26,220
Both of you work
together, you stay strong.

119
00:06:28,355 --> 00:06:31,621
Okay. That's settled.
Thank you. Moving on. Next.

120
00:06:32,259 --> 00:06:33,259
LEE: Wait.

121
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:34,955
How's your daughter?

122
00:06:37,063 --> 00:06:38,622
Fever came down,

123
00:06:40,066 --> 00:06:41,125
thanks to you, Doc.

124
00:06:41,935 --> 00:06:42,959
Good.

125
00:06:48,341 --> 00:06:51,243
These bums are
so lucky to have you.

126
00:06:51,344 --> 00:06:53,677
You cure their children,
you solve their problems.

127
00:06:53,747 --> 00:06:55,215
I haven't forgotten
about you, Ed.

128
00:06:55,415 --> 00:06:58,715
Yes, you say that and
yet I remain a moron.

129
00:06:59,152 --> 00:07:01,712
I said I would
fix you, and I will.

130
00:07:02,122 --> 00:07:03,215
MAN: Out of my way.

131
00:07:03,290 --> 00:07:04,588
Move out of my way.

132
00:07:04,658 --> 00:07:06,593
Out of my way, I
need to see the Doc.

133
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:08,458
What happened?

134
00:07:09,496 --> 00:07:12,625
Sampson sent his thugs to my
shop, demanding protection money.

135
00:07:13,300 --> 00:07:14,393
I told them no.

136
00:07:14,901 --> 00:07:16,392
I said, this is your
neighborhood now.

137
00:07:16,870 --> 00:07:18,031
I'm sorry, who's Sampson?

138
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:19,970
He controls the territory
just south of here.

139
00:07:20,907 --> 00:07:23,035
All right. Go to the
clinic, I'll stitch you up.

140
00:07:25,879 --> 00:07:27,905
You know, this was
bound to happen.

141
00:07:27,981 --> 00:07:29,779
You're new leader
of The Narrows.

142
00:07:30,150 --> 00:07:31,448
Sampson's just testing you.

143
00:07:32,786 --> 00:07:34,948
But you have to show
him, and these people,

144
00:07:35,021 --> 00:07:36,785
that you can't be pushed around.

145
00:07:36,856 --> 00:07:39,087
What, should I send
Grundy to rip his arms off?

146
00:07:39,526 --> 00:07:41,290
Look at him, it's
what he lives for.

147
00:07:42,262 --> 00:07:44,788
I'm asking these people
to settle things amicably.

148
00:07:45,031 --> 00:07:48,433
I can't just be a hypocrite and send
Grundy every time I have a problem.

149
00:07:48,501 --> 00:07:49,594
(SIGHS)

150
00:07:49,970 --> 00:07:51,461
Okay, what would you like to do?

151
00:08:00,981 --> 00:08:02,210
Hello, Sofia.

152
00:08:04,784 --> 00:08:05,784
(STAMMERS)

153
00:08:05,952 --> 00:08:08,512
Oswald, what a
pleasant surprise.

154
00:08:10,223 --> 00:08:12,351
Oh, I assure you, dear,

155
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:17,020
there is nothing
pleasant about it.

156
00:08:17,430 --> 00:08:19,865
I've continually been
suspicious of you.

157
00:08:21,134 --> 00:08:23,797
And yet, at every turn,

158
00:08:23,870 --> 00:08:26,533
you always had the
perfect explanation

159
00:08:26,639 --> 00:08:28,699
to put my mind at ease.

160
00:08:29,676 --> 00:08:30,837
But now,

161
00:08:32,012 --> 00:08:35,847
I finally have proof
that you are my enemy.

162
00:08:37,517 --> 00:08:38,746
You lied to me.

163
00:08:39,819 --> 00:08:41,412
You told me you hated Gordon.

164
00:08:43,690 --> 00:08:44,988
You are his lover.

165
00:08:45,658 --> 00:08:47,820
Martin saw you kissing
him after the party.

166
00:08:49,262 --> 00:08:50,525
That's ridiculous.

167
00:08:50,597 --> 00:08:52,259
I'm not sure what
Martin thought he saw,

168
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:54,095
but I can assure
you it was no kiss...

169
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,498
Enough of your lies!

170
00:08:58,038 --> 00:09:00,530
Our entire friendship,

171
00:09:00,607 --> 00:09:02,906
the intimacies we shared,

172
00:09:03,009 --> 00:09:05,808
they were nothing more
than a pathetic charade.

173
00:09:05,879 --> 00:09:09,043
No, Oswald, I swear. I
swear, I care for you deeply...

174
00:09:09,149 --> 00:09:11,482
Ha! Oh, I wish that were true!

175
00:09:12,352 --> 00:09:14,821
But after Martin told me
about you and Gordon,

176
00:09:14,888 --> 00:09:17,323
I did a little digging
into your boyfriend.

177
00:09:18,658 --> 00:09:21,822
Interesting. He took
a trip down south

178
00:09:21,895 --> 00:09:25,195
shortly before you
arrived in Gotham.

179
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:28,160
Coincidence? I think not.

180
00:09:29,402 --> 00:09:31,268
So you see, I know

181
00:09:31,871 --> 00:09:33,601
that the two of you
have been plotting

182
00:09:33,706 --> 00:09:36,938
to destroy me from
the very beginning.

183
00:09:42,248 --> 00:09:43,546
Bravo, Oswald.

184
00:09:45,318 --> 00:09:47,310
Do you know, I was warned
you were a mastermind?

185
00:09:48,822 --> 00:09:50,120
Turns out you're an easy mark.

186
00:09:50,390 --> 00:09:53,224
It is truly amazing,
what you can accomplish

187
00:09:53,293 --> 00:09:55,728
with goulash and
a good foot rub.

188
00:10:02,602 --> 00:10:04,070
Now I see the real you.

189
00:10:06,606 --> 00:10:07,606
(SNIFFLES)

190
00:10:09,209 --> 00:10:10,700
I was blind to
your manipulations.

191
00:10:11,444 --> 00:10:13,743
But today, I'm going
to correct that mistake.

192
00:10:13,813 --> 00:10:16,442
You will tell me the
full extent of your plan,

193
00:10:16,583 --> 00:10:18,142
if your father was involved,

194
00:10:18,485 --> 00:10:20,215
which of my captains
you have turned

195
00:10:20,653 --> 00:10:22,451
and how you intend
to rid me from this city.

196
00:10:23,389 --> 00:10:24,448
Bring him out.

197
00:10:24,657 --> 00:10:27,491
Allow me to introduce
you to the dentist.

198
00:10:29,062 --> 00:10:31,622
And he is not the kind
who gives out lollipops

199
00:10:31,731 --> 00:10:33,097
after the visit.

200
00:10:44,310 --> 00:10:45,310
(DOOR BUZZES)

201
00:10:45,378 --> 00:10:46,846
Captain Gordon.

202
00:10:47,547 --> 00:10:51,006
I wondered if my little scuffle would
bring you here. I'm so glad it did.

203
00:10:51,351 --> 00:10:53,343
- I've missed our little chats.
- Good.

204
00:10:54,521 --> 00:10:56,649
Then you can start by
telling me who you really are.

205
00:10:58,057 --> 00:10:59,057
Don't you know?

206
00:11:00,994 --> 00:11:03,828
Jim, I'm a reflection of you.

207
00:11:10,370 --> 00:11:11,804
I don't see it.

208
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:14,673
(THE PYG CHUCKLING)

209
00:11:18,044 --> 00:11:20,172
Oh, James, you swine.

210
00:11:24,617 --> 00:11:25,812
(GROANS)

211
00:11:28,388 --> 00:11:30,289
I want to know who's
hiding behind that mask.

212
00:11:31,457 --> 00:11:34,052
What you see is what you get.

213
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:36,857
What I see is someone
who craves attention.

214
00:11:38,131 --> 00:11:40,657
So why are you concealing
your true identity?

215
00:11:40,733 --> 00:11:43,567
Don't you wanna take the
credit for all your brilliant crimes?

216
00:11:43,736 --> 00:11:45,329
Oh, I get all the credit.

217
00:11:45,838 --> 00:11:50,674
The whole town has gone
hog wild for the Pyg. (SNORTS)

218
00:11:51,010 --> 00:11:52,239
Not since I caught you.

219
00:11:52,779 --> 00:11:54,247
You're yesterday's news.

220
00:11:55,782 --> 00:11:57,944
- It's not true.
- This is Gotham.

221
00:11:58,418 --> 00:12:01,513
You're a second-class psychopath
compared to what we've got.

222
00:12:02,255 --> 00:12:05,089
Jerome Valeska,
Fish Mooney, Penguin.

223
00:12:05,792 --> 00:12:09,092
- They have staying power, you don't.
- You're wrong.

224
00:12:10,396 --> 00:12:12,922
I terrified this whole
city for months.

225
00:12:13,766 --> 00:12:16,930
- People will remember that.
- No, they won't.

226
00:12:17,437 --> 00:12:19,997
In fact, they've
already forgotten you.

227
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:24,709
Hmm, but not you,
Jim. You're here.

228
00:12:24,911 --> 00:12:26,038
A final visit.

229
00:12:26,713 --> 00:12:29,342
Now I'm gonna walk out that door
and never think about you again.

230
00:12:30,416 --> 00:12:31,782
(CHUCKLING) Mind games.

231
00:12:33,353 --> 00:12:36,255
You really think that's
going to work on me?

232
00:12:39,025 --> 00:12:40,254
Guard, we're done here.

233
00:12:41,261 --> 00:12:43,560
James, we're not done here.

234
00:12:43,630 --> 00:12:44,791
Have a nice life.

235
00:12:46,566 --> 00:12:49,400
(IN SOUTHERN ACCENT)
Don't you walk out on me!

236
00:12:51,971 --> 00:12:53,803
You'll never forget me.

237
00:12:54,407 --> 00:12:55,898
I promise you that.

238
00:12:57,677 --> 00:12:58,677
There you are.

239
00:13:06,786 --> 00:13:07,845
(DOOR LOCKS)

240
00:13:20,933 --> 00:13:21,933
(GUN COCKING)

241
00:13:27,807 --> 00:13:30,504
So, you're Doc?

242
00:13:31,344 --> 00:13:32,437
I heard you had a giant.

243
00:13:32,512 --> 00:13:33,956
I figured you might have
brought him along with you,

244
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:36,415
rather than this, uh, has-been.

245
00:13:36,482 --> 00:13:37,482
Excuse me.

246
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:43,115
Why would I bring Grundy
along for a friendly conversation?

247
00:13:44,824 --> 00:13:46,535
Look, I understand you
had a deal with Cherry,

248
00:13:46,559 --> 00:13:48,289
where you left her people alone.

249
00:13:49,295 --> 00:13:51,230
I expect you to honor
the same with me.

250
00:13:52,965 --> 00:13:53,989
Why would I do that?

251
00:13:54,734 --> 00:13:56,134
You'e not even from The Narrows.

252
00:13:56,202 --> 00:13:58,797
You have no idea how
things work around here.

253
00:13:59,539 --> 00:14:00,700
Maybe you're right.

254
00:14:00,973 --> 00:14:02,532
But I do know that
you love money.

255
00:14:03,643 --> 00:14:05,669
I'm willing to offer
you 10% of fight night.

256
00:14:06,412 --> 00:14:07,573
You just don't get it, huh?

257
00:14:07,980 --> 00:14:09,073
I'm not negotiating.

258
00:14:09,582 --> 00:14:10,641
I'm taking.

259
00:14:11,150 --> 00:14:12,345
I'm taking your clinic.

260
00:14:13,353 --> 00:14:14,548
I'm taking your club.

261
00:14:15,988 --> 00:14:17,616
I'm taking your whole
damn neighborhood.

262
00:14:20,193 --> 00:14:23,288
Okay, we tried this your
way. Let's use Grundy.

263
00:14:23,996 --> 00:14:25,157
(COUGHING)

264
00:14:27,900 --> 00:14:29,334
That doesn't sound so good.

265
00:14:30,470 --> 00:14:31,995
You cough up blood yet?

266
00:14:32,572 --> 00:14:33,572
What's it to you?

267
00:14:34,073 --> 00:14:35,666
Bad case of Narrows
Lung going around.

268
00:14:36,642 --> 00:14:37,803
What the hell is that?

269
00:14:38,411 --> 00:14:39,470
It's a new virus.

270
00:14:39,879 --> 00:14:41,472
I've seen it kill a
few people already.

271
00:14:42,081 --> 00:14:44,414
First you cough up blood and
within a few days you're dead.

272
00:14:44,517 --> 00:14:45,644
Unless you have treatment.

273
00:14:46,586 --> 00:14:49,681
I'll sweeten the deal. I will
doctor your people, free of charge.

274
00:14:50,089 --> 00:14:51,352
(LAUGHING)

275
00:14:52,191 --> 00:14:53,921
Not gonna get a
better offer than that.

276
00:14:54,394 --> 00:14:56,124
(LAUGHING TURNS TO COUGHING)

277
00:14:58,531 --> 00:14:59,555
All right.

278
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:01,698
I'll be back in a few days

279
00:15:01,768 --> 00:15:03,737
to negotiate with
whoever takes your place,

280
00:15:04,237 --> 00:15:06,069
after you drown
in your own blood.

281
00:15:10,543 --> 00:15:11,806
Tell you what, Doc.

282
00:15:13,212 --> 00:15:14,976
Make it 30% of fight night,

283
00:15:16,048 --> 00:15:17,107
you got yourself a deal.

284
00:15:17,216 --> 00:15:18,616
It's too much, don't take it.

285
00:15:19,385 --> 00:15:20,717
(COUGHING)

286
00:15:24,223 --> 00:15:25,452
Come by the clinic later.

287
00:15:26,058 --> 00:15:27,253
We'll see about that cough.

288
00:15:28,795 --> 00:15:29,795
(GROANING)

289
00:15:33,266 --> 00:15:35,758
Your teeth are quite lovely.

290
00:15:36,569 --> 00:15:38,697
I look forward to putting
them in my trophy case.

291
00:15:40,873 --> 00:15:42,899
You have no idea
who I am, do you?

292
00:15:43,109 --> 00:15:44,202
Of course, I do.

293
00:15:44,277 --> 00:15:46,576
You are Don Falcone's daughter.

294
00:15:48,748 --> 00:15:50,080
He killed my brother.

295
00:15:51,017 --> 00:15:52,645
(WHIRRING)

296
00:15:53,419 --> 00:15:54,910
I'm going to enjoy this.

297
00:15:56,289 --> 00:15:57,733
SOFIA: It's true he
killed your brother,

298
00:15:57,757 --> 00:16:00,852
but not your wife, Elaine,
or your son, Joseph.

299
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:03,452
No, they're still alive,
probably having lunch

300
00:16:03,529 --> 00:16:05,691
in your two-bedroom
on 7th Ave right now.

301
00:16:05,798 --> 00:16:07,323
(WHIRRING STOPS)

302
00:16:10,336 --> 00:16:13,033
See, I made it a point
to learn every detail

303
00:16:13,139 --> 00:16:14,630
of Penguin's organization.

304
00:16:15,107 --> 00:16:19,101
For instance, I learned that he only
trusts one man for this type of job.

305
00:16:19,278 --> 00:16:20,278
You.

306
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:22,640
And in the event that
I am ever tortured,

307
00:16:22,748 --> 00:16:24,580
my people have instructions

308
00:16:25,151 --> 00:16:26,619
to kill your family.

309
00:16:27,954 --> 00:16:29,684
Interesting threat.

310
00:16:30,923 --> 00:16:33,017
But no one's going to
know that you were tortured.

311
00:16:34,193 --> 00:16:36,287
Because no one is
going to find your body.

312
00:16:36,429 --> 00:16:39,957
Oh! 'Cause you don't think I have
spies inside Penguin's organization?

313
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:41,920
He's right about me, though.

314
00:16:41,968 --> 00:16:43,994
I have been conspiring
against him for months,

315
00:16:44,103 --> 00:16:46,368
turning his captains
against him one by one.

316
00:16:46,472 --> 00:16:51,103
And today is the day that
I will finally take him down.

317
00:16:51,577 --> 00:16:54,547
So, if my people don't
hear from me soon,

318
00:16:55,481 --> 00:16:56,881
your family's dead.

319
00:16:59,385 --> 00:17:00,683
But if you don't believe me,

320
00:17:02,021 --> 00:17:03,045
drill away.

321
00:17:05,391 --> 00:17:06,723
Excuse me,

322
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:09,090
her restraints need tightening.

323
00:17:16,002 --> 00:17:17,834
- (DRILL WHIRRING)
- (MAN SCREAMING)

324
00:17:24,143 --> 00:17:26,078
Hmm. A wise decision.

325
00:17:28,180 --> 00:17:29,478
Now, untie me.

326
00:17:44,897 --> 00:17:45,897
(WHIMPERING)

327
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:48,993
Things are finally looking up.

328
00:17:54,073 --> 00:17:55,632
- BARBARA: Wakey, wakey.
- (GASPS)

329
00:17:57,443 --> 00:17:58,706
Oh, hello.

330
00:17:59,412 --> 00:18:01,574
I don't believe we've
met. I'm Barbara Kean.

331
00:18:01,647 --> 00:18:03,445
This ferocious lady
is Tabitha Galavan

332
00:18:03,549 --> 00:18:06,280
and that kitty cat,
that's Selina Kyle.

333
00:18:07,219 --> 00:18:08,585
I know who you are.

334
00:18:09,388 --> 00:18:11,880
Penguin wants you dead for
betraying him down in The Narrows.

335
00:18:12,825 --> 00:18:14,123
What do you want with me?

336
00:18:14,327 --> 00:18:17,092
Well, we heard you
and Ozzy are BFFs.

337
00:18:18,664 --> 00:18:22,465
So, you're going to try and leverage
me to get Penguin not to kill you.

338
00:18:23,102 --> 00:18:24,542
TABITHA: We have
some other demands.

339
00:18:24,570 --> 00:18:26,129
But essentially, yeah.

340
00:18:26,405 --> 00:18:27,600
That's a good plan,

341
00:18:27,707 --> 00:18:30,404
except for the fact that
Penguin just tried to kill me.

342
00:18:31,277 --> 00:18:32,609
Why would he do that?

343
00:18:33,946 --> 00:18:37,314
Because I am so close to
taking his underworld from him.

344
00:18:37,750 --> 00:18:38,750
(SELINA SCOFFS)

345
00:18:40,319 --> 00:18:41,319
You're lying.

346
00:18:41,787 --> 00:18:42,787
SOFIA: Am I?

347
00:18:43,589 --> 00:18:46,115
I've been working
Penguin for months,

348
00:18:46,292 --> 00:18:49,990
manipulating him into behaving
exactly how I want him to.

349
00:18:50,096 --> 00:18:53,328
Every move he made
today, I orchestrated.

350
00:18:54,567 --> 00:18:57,196
Now you three are
screwing things up.

351
00:18:58,704 --> 00:19:01,765
So, you want him out
of your life, let me go.

352
00:19:07,780 --> 00:19:09,442
(WHISPERS) Maybe
she's telling the truth.

353
00:19:10,316 --> 00:19:11,682
She's a Falcone.

354
00:19:12,385 --> 00:19:14,684
She learned to lie
before she could read.

355
00:19:15,287 --> 00:19:19,054
But whether you are friend or
foe makes no difference to me,

356
00:19:19,392 --> 00:19:21,554
because Penguin
will still make the deal.

357
00:19:22,228 --> 00:19:23,787
Get him on the phone.

358
00:19:32,438 --> 00:19:33,438
You'll grow into it.

359
00:19:33,606 --> 00:19:34,767
(PENGUIN LAUGHS)

360
00:19:36,509 --> 00:19:40,276
Because of you, I was
able to vanquish my enemy.

361
00:19:41,280 --> 00:19:43,840
And now that you've
proven yourself,

362
00:19:44,784 --> 00:19:47,720
I see a beautiful
future ahead for you.

363
00:19:49,488 --> 00:19:52,287
I have so much wisdom to impart.

364
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:55,653
And if you pay attention,

365
00:19:56,829 --> 00:19:58,923
one day all of this
could be yours.

366
00:20:01,434 --> 00:20:02,434
What's wrong?

367
00:20:17,950 --> 00:20:19,043
What are you talking about?

368
00:20:21,554 --> 00:20:25,389
You mean, you did not
see Sofia kissing Gordon?

369
00:20:41,941 --> 00:20:43,102
Why would she do that?

370
00:20:44,543 --> 00:20:45,738
Unless...

371
00:20:47,513 --> 00:20:50,244
She knew exactly
how I would respond.

372
00:20:52,184 --> 00:20:54,346
She wanted me to confront her.

373
00:20:55,354 --> 00:20:56,788
Even torture her.

374
00:20:57,356 --> 00:20:59,757
Boss, we have a problem.

375
00:20:59,859 --> 00:21:01,122
The dentist is gone.

376
00:21:02,161 --> 00:21:03,595
What happened to Sofia?

377
00:21:03,662 --> 00:21:05,426
To be honest, that's
still a little unclear.

378
00:21:05,765 --> 00:21:07,256
Barbara Kean has her.

379
00:21:07,466 --> 00:21:09,833
What? How do you know this?

380
00:21:10,069 --> 00:21:11,935
She's on the phone.

381
00:21:12,905 --> 00:21:14,134
Says she wants to make a deal.

382
00:21:15,274 --> 00:21:16,936
Give me that.

383
00:21:19,345 --> 00:21:20,404
Barbara.

384
00:21:20,479 --> 00:21:21,970
Hello, Oswald.

385
00:21:22,148 --> 00:21:25,846
I see you have crawled out from
whatever rock you were hiding under.

386
00:21:27,086 --> 00:21:28,520
What are you doing with Sofia?

387
00:21:28,621 --> 00:21:29,919
We scooped her up this morning.

388
00:21:30,456 --> 00:21:33,290
And of course, when we did, we
thought she was your best friend.

389
00:21:33,392 --> 00:21:35,759
Turns out, she's
your worst enemy.

390
00:21:36,562 --> 00:21:38,997
I want her back.
Name your price.

391
00:21:39,165 --> 00:21:41,794
We keep the gun shop,
we don't share profits

392
00:21:41,901 --> 00:21:45,770
and from this point forward we
operate with complete autonomy.

393
00:21:46,839 --> 00:21:48,068
Fine.

394
00:21:48,808 --> 00:21:50,834
I will send Zsasz
over to collect her.

395
00:21:51,477 --> 00:21:53,639
She had better be
there when he arrives.

396
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:54,979
She will be.

397
00:22:07,293 --> 00:22:09,194
And as for you, young man,

398
00:22:10,129 --> 00:22:12,997
our conversation is not over.

399
00:22:16,969 --> 00:22:18,969
GORDON: So, this is what
the Pyg used to look like?

400
00:22:19,038 --> 00:22:20,038
That's him.

401
00:22:20,372 --> 00:22:22,864
All right, send it out to police
stations across the country.

402
00:22:22,975 --> 00:22:25,137
- Start in the South.
- The South? Why?

403
00:22:25,211 --> 00:22:27,476
When I pressed him, he
spoke in a Southern accent.

404
00:22:27,746 --> 00:22:29,825
He could have done that
deliberately to throw you off.

405
00:22:29,849 --> 00:22:31,579
No, he slipped up.

406
00:22:31,884 --> 00:22:33,079
I saw it in his eyes.

407
00:22:33,185 --> 00:22:34,619
This is the best lead we've got.

408
00:22:34,854 --> 00:22:36,379
Let's see where it goes.

409
00:22:40,893 --> 00:22:42,093
NYGMA: I don't understand you.

410
00:22:42,161 --> 00:22:44,858
If Sampson's cough will
kill him, why not let him die?

411
00:22:45,331 --> 00:22:47,129
There's no such thing
as Narrow's Lung.

412
00:22:47,333 --> 00:22:48,699
He probably just has bronchitis.

413
00:22:49,001 --> 00:22:51,334
I give him some medicine,
he feels better, problem solved.

414
00:22:51,537 --> 00:22:53,165
Okay, what about the 30%?

415
00:22:53,239 --> 00:22:55,003
Once he has that, he's
just gonna want more.

416
00:22:55,074 --> 00:22:56,074
Maybe.

417
00:23:12,758 --> 00:23:15,023
Sampson, you son of a bitch.

418
00:23:16,929 --> 00:23:18,522
Now do you see who
you're dealing with?

419
00:23:21,533 --> 00:23:23,092
I know you wanted
to try this your way.

420
00:23:24,803 --> 00:23:26,465
No more diplomacy, Lee.

421
00:23:27,106 --> 00:23:29,541
Take Grundy and end this.

422
00:23:31,810 --> 00:23:32,810
No.

423
00:23:33,646 --> 00:23:34,909
I have a better idea.

424
00:23:36,482 --> 00:23:39,247
- That was easy.
- Yeah, a little too easy.

425
00:23:40,352 --> 00:23:42,592
SOFIA: Because he couldn't
wait to get you off the phone.

426
00:23:42,788 --> 00:23:44,552
We need to get out of here.

427
00:23:45,524 --> 00:23:46,856
And then what happens?

428
00:23:47,559 --> 00:23:49,027
You take over from Penguin?

429
00:23:50,262 --> 00:23:53,130
We are not working for
anyone but ourselves.

430
00:23:54,099 --> 00:23:55,727
I'm not asking you to.

431
00:23:56,735 --> 00:23:59,466
I will give you everything
you want from Penguin.

432
00:24:00,306 --> 00:24:02,571
You're not in a position
to offer us anything.

433
00:24:03,208 --> 00:24:04,232
We're in charge here.

434
00:24:04,310 --> 00:24:06,370
Uh, guys, I think we
should listen to her.

435
00:24:06,445 --> 00:24:07,445
Why?

436
00:24:07,546 --> 00:24:10,448
Because Zsasz is standing out
front holding a rocket launcher.

437
00:24:13,085 --> 00:24:14,085
Ladies.

438
00:24:20,092 --> 00:24:21,151
(LAUGHING)

439
00:24:23,262 --> 00:24:25,254
(ALL COUGHING)

440
00:24:29,535 --> 00:24:32,369
I'm gonna break
his little beak in half.

441
00:24:37,209 --> 00:24:38,209
SOFIA: Jim.

442
00:24:38,444 --> 00:24:41,004
Sorry, Captain. I tried to stop
her. I told her she had to wait.

443
00:24:41,513 --> 00:24:43,175
It's okay,
Detective. I've got it.

444
00:24:43,649 --> 00:24:45,584
Sofia, what happened to you?

445
00:24:46,151 --> 00:24:47,642
I underestimated Oswald.

446
00:24:47,987 --> 00:24:49,615
He found out we were
plotting against him

447
00:24:49,688 --> 00:24:51,247
and he just tried
to kill me, Jim.

448
00:24:51,490 --> 00:24:52,685
He can't hurt you here.

449
00:24:53,192 --> 00:24:55,354
If he finds out I'm alive,
he will come after me

450
00:24:55,461 --> 00:24:57,589
and he won't
stop until I'm dead.

451
00:24:57,997 --> 00:25:01,195
You are the Captain of the GCPD,
your men would follow you anywhere.

452
00:25:01,300 --> 00:25:04,964
Please, please, use the
position I gave you and end this.

453
00:25:05,804 --> 00:25:06,999
What are you proposing I do?

454
00:25:07,506 --> 00:25:10,203
You have an army, just
take the fight to Penguin.

455
00:25:13,212 --> 00:25:14,475
So, this was your plan.

456
00:25:15,681 --> 00:25:16,876
To start a war.

457
00:25:18,717 --> 00:25:21,551
You knew you didn't have the
numbers to fight Penguin on your own,

458
00:25:21,653 --> 00:25:23,815
so you made me Captain,
knowing it would come to this,

459
00:25:23,889 --> 00:25:25,050
and I'd take him out for you.

460
00:25:25,157 --> 00:25:27,717
Your job is to stop
criminals, Jim, here you go.

461
00:25:27,826 --> 00:25:29,522
It is not that simple,
and you know it.

462
00:25:31,230 --> 00:25:33,529
We could bring law and
order back to Gotham.

463
00:25:34,867 --> 00:25:36,978
This is exactly what you asked
for when you came down south

464
00:25:37,002 --> 00:25:38,994
and it is yours for the taking.

465
00:25:39,738 --> 00:25:41,331
You know what
has to be done, Jim.

466
00:25:42,174 --> 00:25:43,506
Crush Penguin.

467
00:25:52,885 --> 00:25:54,410
I trusted you, Martin.

468
00:25:55,354 --> 00:25:56,720
And you betrayed me.

469
00:26:07,399 --> 00:26:09,595
I think it's time for you to
go back to the orphanage.

470
00:26:11,403 --> 00:26:12,632
- Boss.
- Hold on.

471
00:26:14,540 --> 00:26:17,032
Let the little spy
step out of the room.

472
00:26:27,920 --> 00:26:28,920
So?

473
00:26:29,755 --> 00:26:32,486
The place went up
like a great ball of fire.

474
00:26:32,891 --> 00:26:35,292
Good. Alert the capos.

475
00:26:35,894 --> 00:26:40,059
We are going to unleash a crime
wave on this city like it has never seen.

476
00:26:40,732 --> 00:26:42,064
That will teach Jim Gordon

477
00:26:42,134 --> 00:26:44,126
to align himself
with Sofia Falcone.

478
00:26:44,236 --> 00:26:46,116
GORDON: I wouldn't
make that call if I were you.

479
00:26:47,306 --> 00:26:48,535
I just spoke with Sofia.

480
00:26:49,875 --> 00:26:51,036
She's alive.

481
00:26:51,110 --> 00:26:53,136
And she told me
you tried to kill her.

482
00:26:54,046 --> 00:26:55,139
Hearsay, Jim.

483
00:26:55,481 --> 00:26:57,450
Been here all day.
I have witnesses.

484
00:26:57,616 --> 00:26:58,640
I don't care.

485
00:27:00,619 --> 00:27:01,780
I'm not here to arrest you.

486
00:27:03,422 --> 00:27:04,651
I came to make a deal.

487
00:27:05,457 --> 00:27:07,756
I think we've both put
up with Sofia long enough.

488
00:27:10,829 --> 00:27:12,422
Victor, would you
give us a moment?

489
00:27:16,702 --> 00:27:18,830
Okay, Jim. You
have my attention.

490
00:27:20,205 --> 00:27:22,197
Since the moment
she set foot in Gotham,

491
00:27:22,307 --> 00:27:24,776
Sofia has put us
on a path to war.

492
00:27:25,210 --> 00:27:27,202
She's willing to let this
city burn to the ground

493
00:27:27,312 --> 00:27:28,610
to prove herself to her father.

494
00:27:28,814 --> 00:27:29,838
I can't allow that.

495
00:27:31,316 --> 00:27:32,784
So, what do you want from me?

496
00:27:33,819 --> 00:27:35,720
I'm putting her on
a train home tonight.

497
00:27:36,188 --> 00:27:38,348
But I need assurances from
you, you won't get involved.

498
00:27:39,224 --> 00:27:40,317
Not good enough.

499
00:27:40,792 --> 00:27:43,159
She needs to suffer
for what she has done.

500
00:27:43,228 --> 00:27:44,287
That is not gonna happen.

501
00:27:44,363 --> 00:27:46,423
And how do you think
your girlfriend's gonna react

502
00:27:46,498 --> 00:27:47,989
when she realizes
you betrayed her?

503
00:27:48,834 --> 00:27:50,826
You think she's just
gonna run away quietly?

504
00:27:51,136 --> 00:27:54,629
If she sets foot in Gotham
again, I'll put her behind bars.

505
00:27:58,010 --> 00:27:59,034
And if I say no?

506
00:27:59,845 --> 00:28:01,279
Then I'll have no choice

507
00:28:02,047 --> 00:28:04,846
but to use the full
force of the GCPD

508
00:28:05,450 --> 00:28:06,474
to tear you apart,

509
00:28:06,785 --> 00:28:09,516
piece by piece.

510
00:28:10,989 --> 00:28:12,349
That does not
sound very pleasant.

511
00:28:12,391 --> 00:28:13,791
It won't be.

512
00:28:16,395 --> 00:28:18,694
I guess I can put aside
my personal feelings

513
00:28:18,764 --> 00:28:20,392
for the good of this city.

514
00:28:20,699 --> 00:28:22,930
But I do have one
question for you, Jim.

515
00:28:23,835 --> 00:28:25,428
When Sofia is gone,

516
00:28:26,572 --> 00:28:27,665
where does that leave us?

517
00:28:28,440 --> 00:28:29,738
No more licenses.

518
00:28:30,442 --> 00:28:32,707
If you or any other criminal
in this city break the law,

519
00:28:32,778 --> 00:28:34,041
my men will enforce it.

520
00:28:35,280 --> 00:28:37,440
But at least you won't have
to worry about Sofia again.

521
00:28:39,051 --> 00:28:41,782
So, do we have a deal?

522
00:28:44,723 --> 00:28:46,749
After all we have been
through together, Jim,

523
00:28:46,959 --> 00:28:49,895
it is nice that we can resolve
this matter with diplomacy.

524
00:28:59,705 --> 00:29:01,003
(SAMPSON BURPING)

525
00:29:01,506 --> 00:29:02,735
Doc.

526
00:29:03,709 --> 00:29:05,610
I heard about what
happened to your clinic.

527
00:29:06,078 --> 00:29:07,102
What a shame.

528
00:29:07,346 --> 00:29:11,408
I was looking forward to
you curing my Narrows Lung.

529
00:29:11,516 --> 00:29:13,007
(LAUGHING)

530
00:29:15,254 --> 00:29:17,614
I want you cleared out of The
Narrows by the end of the day.

531
00:29:18,924 --> 00:29:21,164
- What did you say to me?
- I think she was pretty clear.

532
00:29:23,629 --> 00:29:24,995
Well, allow me to be clear.

533
00:29:26,131 --> 00:29:28,066
This is my turf and
I'm not going anywhere.

534
00:29:28,133 --> 00:29:29,965
And you two have
dug your own graves.

535
00:29:30,135 --> 00:29:31,899
Oh, well, then I guess
you don't want this.

536
00:29:34,072 --> 00:29:35,096
What's that?

537
00:29:35,507 --> 00:29:36,547
The antidote to the poison

538
00:29:36,608 --> 00:29:38,804
I had slipped in your
drink about 30 minutes ago.

539
00:29:40,979 --> 00:29:42,140
Ironic, isn't it?

540
00:29:42,748 --> 00:29:45,343
It's the only thing from the
clinic that wasn't destroyed,

541
00:29:45,751 --> 00:29:48,915
some vials of medicine I had
mixed into a deadly combination.

542
00:29:48,987 --> 00:29:51,149
It should be kicking
in right about now.

543
00:29:52,591 --> 00:29:55,060
You're bluffing. I feel
absolutely fine. (GROANS)

544
00:29:55,761 --> 00:29:56,888
I'm sorry, what was that?

545
00:29:57,796 --> 00:29:58,820
Get them.

546
00:29:59,731 --> 00:30:01,411
LEE: Come any closer
and I'll destroy this.

547
00:30:02,301 --> 00:30:03,301
(SAMPSON COUGHING)

548
00:30:12,010 --> 00:30:13,010
Like I said,

549
00:30:13,945 --> 00:30:16,608
leave by the end of
the day and you live.

550
00:30:18,750 --> 00:30:19,750
Deal?

551
00:30:23,021 --> 00:30:24,021
Oh!

552
00:30:24,356 --> 00:30:25,380
Catch.

553
00:30:28,393 --> 00:30:29,827
(COUGHING INTENSIFIES)

554
00:30:33,865 --> 00:30:36,460
I know you're disappointed,
but I am doing this to protect you.

555
00:30:36,635 --> 00:30:38,536
Disappointment doesn't
quite cover it, Jim.

556
00:30:38,637 --> 00:30:40,572
If you stay in Gotham,
Penguin will kill you.

557
00:30:40,672 --> 00:30:41,731
Don't put this on Penguin.

558
00:30:42,341 --> 00:30:44,572
If you have something to
say, I think you should say it.

559
00:30:55,721 --> 00:30:56,780
We're the same, Jim.

560
00:30:58,790 --> 00:31:00,782
I saw it the first
moment we met.

561
00:31:01,727 --> 00:31:02,820
We both want power.

562
00:31:03,895 --> 00:31:05,830
You want to deny
it, but it's true.

563
00:31:05,897 --> 00:31:08,298
And it is just easier
to send me away.

564
00:31:12,237 --> 00:31:13,237
(HANDCUFFS CLICKING)

565
00:31:15,006 --> 00:31:17,874
Detective Harper, please take
Miss Falcone to the train station

566
00:31:18,210 --> 00:31:19,542
and escort her back home.

567
00:31:20,545 --> 00:31:21,545
Please, don't do this.

568
00:31:21,847 --> 00:31:22,847
Better get going.

569
00:31:23,348 --> 00:31:24,407
You'll miss your train.

570
00:31:32,758 --> 00:31:34,351
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

571
00:31:37,129 --> 00:31:38,597
ZSASZ: Gordon
put her on the train.

572
00:31:39,898 --> 00:31:41,457
Talk about a turn of events.

573
00:31:42,067 --> 00:31:43,228
I did not see that coming.

574
00:31:44,970 --> 00:31:48,134
What about the kid? You want me
to take him back to the orphanage?

575
00:31:53,078 --> 00:31:54,307
That won't be necessary.

576
00:31:57,949 --> 00:31:59,884
Martin, I have been thinking.

577
00:32:00,952 --> 00:32:02,011
I was angry.

578
00:32:02,421 --> 00:32:03,445
I did not mean what I...

579
00:32:05,724 --> 00:32:06,748
Martin.

580
00:32:21,606 --> 00:32:22,904
Martin.

581
00:32:26,945 --> 00:32:27,945
(CAR DOOR OPENING)

582
00:32:31,149 --> 00:32:32,149
BARBARA: Aw!

583
00:32:32,484 --> 00:32:33,611
He's cute.

584
00:32:34,119 --> 00:32:35,143
He doesn't talk.

585
00:32:38,356 --> 00:32:39,824
Kid gives me the creeps.

586
00:32:42,661 --> 00:32:43,959
Let's get this over with.

587
00:33:01,480 --> 00:33:02,607
Nervous about something?

588
00:33:04,282 --> 00:33:06,012
Well, we have a long way to go.

589
00:33:06,485 --> 00:33:07,509
So, get comfy.

590
00:33:15,293 --> 00:33:16,317
MAN: Tickets, please.

591
00:33:16,495 --> 00:33:17,929
(GASPS) What...

592
00:33:19,498 --> 00:33:20,498
(GUN COCKING)

593
00:33:23,635 --> 00:33:25,604
- Hello, Victor.
- Where's the boy?

594
00:33:25,971 --> 00:33:27,269
Alive, for now.

595
00:33:28,540 --> 00:33:30,202
If Oswald wants
to keep it that way,

596
00:33:30,308 --> 00:33:33,210
he will meet me under the
Crown Point Bridge in one hour.

597
00:33:33,311 --> 00:33:34,951
CONDUCTOR: (ON PA)
<i>Next stop, Stevenstown.</i>

598
00:33:35,413 --> 00:33:36,506
It's my stop.

599
00:33:37,682 --> 00:33:38,809
Do you mind?

600
00:33:39,918 --> 00:33:41,011
Not at all.

601
00:33:43,488 --> 00:33:44,547
Thank you.

602
00:34:10,315 --> 00:34:11,840
Glad you could make it, Oswald.

603
00:34:13,985 --> 00:34:16,011
Everything will be all
right, Martin, I promise.

604
00:34:17,689 --> 00:34:19,157
Well, that depends on you.

605
00:34:19,991 --> 00:34:21,857
Turn over control of
the underworld to me

606
00:34:21,927 --> 00:34:25,386
and I'll let little Martin
here keep his head.

607
00:34:27,933 --> 00:34:30,767
The name Falcone used to
mean something in this town.

608
00:34:31,469 --> 00:34:35,133
Wait until your
father hears of this.

609
00:34:35,240 --> 00:34:38,210
Threatening the life of a
child? He will be disgusted.

610
00:34:38,276 --> 00:34:39,539
Wrong.

611
00:34:40,412 --> 00:34:42,210
My father will be proud.

612
00:34:46,051 --> 00:34:48,577
Must be hard to
live your whole life

613
00:34:48,653 --> 00:34:51,122
trying to get Daddy's approval.

614
00:34:51,222 --> 00:34:52,815
I, myself, can't relate,

615
00:34:52,924 --> 00:34:56,588
seeing as my parents
loved me without condition.

616
00:34:59,264 --> 00:35:02,132
Say one more word
and I will kill him

617
00:35:02,233 --> 00:35:04,065
and then I will execute you.

618
00:35:04,903 --> 00:35:06,235
I am choosing compassion,

619
00:35:06,304 --> 00:35:08,432
but I am willing to
change my position.

620
00:35:14,646 --> 00:35:15,646
Don't hurt the boy.

621
00:35:16,948 --> 00:35:17,948
He's innocent.

622
00:35:24,289 --> 00:35:25,313
I submit!

623
00:35:27,158 --> 00:35:28,158
(WHISPERING) Go ahead.

624
00:35:36,434 --> 00:35:37,959
Martin, I want you to know,

625
00:35:39,204 --> 00:35:40,672
I am sorry for
what I said today.

626
00:35:42,440 --> 00:35:43,840
I do care about you.

627
00:35:45,710 --> 00:35:47,178
You know that's true, don't you?

628
00:35:51,282 --> 00:35:52,341
Good.

629
00:35:54,886 --> 00:35:57,685
Now, go wait in the car.

630
00:36:20,545 --> 00:36:22,138
You were wise to use the boy.

631
00:36:23,548 --> 00:36:24,641
As you know,

632
00:36:25,183 --> 00:36:27,709
my heart is my
greatest weakness.

633
00:36:31,723 --> 00:36:35,455
But I will not allow him
to be used as a pawn

634
00:36:35,527 --> 00:36:38,429
in your game anymore.

635
00:36:43,568 --> 00:36:44,568
(GASPS)

636
00:36:54,913 --> 00:36:56,279
You wanted a war,

637
00:36:56,948 --> 00:36:58,712
you've got one!

638
00:37:14,065 --> 00:37:16,398
Ed, why so blue?

639
00:37:16,668 --> 00:37:17,897
We had a great day.

640
00:37:18,069 --> 00:37:19,367
You had a great day.

641
00:37:20,071 --> 00:37:21,403
I did nothing to help.

642
00:37:21,940 --> 00:37:22,940
That's not true.

643
00:37:23,775 --> 00:37:24,852
I couldn't have
done it without you.

644
00:37:24,876 --> 00:37:27,675
I'm not meant to
be a sidekick, Lee.

645
00:37:32,083 --> 00:37:34,712
Sampson is right.
I'm a has-been.

646
00:37:37,422 --> 00:37:38,446
No, you're not.

647
00:37:40,258 --> 00:37:43,126
Look, I asked you to trust me
with something today, and you did.

648
00:37:43,728 --> 00:37:45,321
So, I'm gonna trust
you with something.

649
00:37:47,565 --> 00:37:49,830
I haven't been looking for
a cure for your brain, Ed,

650
00:37:50,468 --> 00:37:52,061
because there's
nothing wrong with you.

651
00:37:53,438 --> 00:37:54,497
- But you...
- Sure,

652
00:37:54,606 --> 00:37:56,598
at first there was an
effect from the ice.

653
00:37:57,575 --> 00:37:59,407
But I ran all the
tests, checks out.

654
00:38:00,411 --> 00:38:02,073
There's nothing wrong
with you physically.

655
00:38:02,413 --> 00:38:03,813
Your condition is psychological.

656
00:38:05,784 --> 00:38:06,808
Think about it.

657
00:38:07,352 --> 00:38:09,651
You knew every move that
Sampson was gonna make

658
00:38:09,754 --> 00:38:10,983
before he made it.

659
00:38:13,591 --> 00:38:14,752
You lied to me.

660
00:38:16,594 --> 00:38:17,721
Why?

661
00:38:18,263 --> 00:38:20,107
Because I was afraid
that if I told you the truth,

662
00:38:20,131 --> 00:38:22,225
you would go back to
being who you were before.

663
00:38:22,500 --> 00:38:23,500
The Riddler.

664
00:38:24,102 --> 00:38:25,798
And I like who you've become.

665
00:38:27,806 --> 00:38:28,933
Who's that?

666
00:38:31,442 --> 00:38:32,637
Ed Nygma.

667
00:38:34,245 --> 00:38:35,645
The Ed that you were before.

668
00:38:37,515 --> 00:38:38,676
My friend.

669
00:38:45,824 --> 00:38:47,053
Well, that backfired.

670
00:38:47,392 --> 00:38:49,503
Penguin's gonna be coming
for us. What are we gonna do?

671
00:38:49,527 --> 00:38:50,995
We hit him before he hits us.

672
00:38:52,163 --> 00:38:53,495
Lady, you lost.

673
00:38:54,132 --> 00:38:55,623
Penguin just blew up that kid.

674
00:38:56,201 --> 00:38:57,533
I admit I didn't
see that coming.

675
00:38:57,635 --> 00:39:00,195
But Oswald still has to align
his capos before he moves on us.

676
00:39:00,305 --> 00:39:02,297
We use that window
of time to make our play.

677
00:39:03,641 --> 00:39:06,008
You didn't get told "no"
a lot as a kid, did you?

678
00:39:06,578 --> 00:39:08,206
You took your shot
and you missed.

679
00:39:08,546 --> 00:39:09,809
We're going it alone from here.

680
00:39:09,981 --> 00:39:10,981
You leave now,

681
00:39:11,349 --> 00:39:13,109
and you will never
have a piece of this city.

682
00:39:16,688 --> 00:39:18,520
Now, that sounded like a threat.

683
00:39:19,023 --> 00:39:22,892
Your club is destroyed. You
have nowhere else to turn.

684
00:39:23,361 --> 00:39:24,385
You need me.

685
00:39:25,630 --> 00:39:28,031
Penguin may have won the battle,

686
00:39:28,566 --> 00:39:30,330
but tomorrow, we win the war.

687
00:39:33,171 --> 00:39:34,171
ZSASZ: Boss.

688
00:39:43,548 --> 00:39:44,548
My boy,

689
00:39:45,383 --> 00:39:47,545
you did a splendid job of dying.

690
00:39:56,895 --> 00:39:59,194
Victor will take you
to a safe location.

691
00:40:00,531 --> 00:40:02,295
You can never return to Gotham.

692
00:40:04,736 --> 00:40:06,364
This is goodbye, my friend.

693
00:40:18,416 --> 00:40:19,440
There, there.

694
00:40:21,352 --> 00:40:23,014
This is what I have
to do to protect you.

695
00:40:23,354 --> 00:40:25,414
One day, when you're
older, you will understand.

696
00:40:37,869 --> 00:40:39,770
Sofia's on our heels, boss.

697
00:40:40,038 --> 00:40:41,038
Let's finish her off.

698
00:40:41,606 --> 00:40:42,972
Have someone else take the kid.

699
00:40:43,875 --> 00:40:46,435
No! I want my top man on this.

700
00:40:47,278 --> 00:40:51,648
Besides, I have something much
better planned for Sofia Falcone.

701
00:40:56,287 --> 00:40:57,482
You were right about the Pyg.

702
00:40:57,956 --> 00:41:00,289
A precinct down south
recognized the picture

703
00:41:00,358 --> 00:41:01,485
you had me send out.

704
00:41:01,659 --> 00:41:03,628
His real name is
Lazlo Valentine.

705
00:41:03,861 --> 00:41:04,920
What do we know about him?

706
00:41:05,163 --> 00:41:07,860
He was being held for a string of
murders down there 10 years ago.

707
00:41:07,966 --> 00:41:08,966
But here's the thing.

708
00:41:09,033 --> 00:41:11,525
His previous victims
weren't police officers

709
00:41:11,636 --> 00:41:13,628
and there was no Pyg persona.

710
00:41:14,605 --> 00:41:16,506
Serial killers don't
usually change their MO.

711
00:41:16,674 --> 00:41:17,733
This guy did.

712
00:41:18,910 --> 00:41:20,606
You said he was being held.

713
00:41:21,679 --> 00:41:23,341
Did they say why
their case fell apart?

714
00:41:23,448 --> 00:41:25,110
It didn't. He escaped.

715
00:41:27,752 --> 00:41:29,983
Call Arkham. Have them
put a guard on his cell.

716
00:41:30,088 --> 00:41:31,147
I'm on my way.

717
00:41:39,630 --> 00:41:40,859
(METALLIC SCRAPING)

718
00:41:44,168 --> 00:41:45,168
Pyg?

719
00:41:53,411 --> 00:41:54,674
(SCRAPING CONTINUES)

720
00:42:02,487 --> 00:42:03,887
Pyg!

721
00:42:09,660 --> 00:42:11,856
(CHOKING)

722
00:42:29,747 --> 00:42:30,747
(GASPS)

723
00:42:31,015 --> 00:42:32,984
- Hello, Ed.
- No.

724
00:42:34,352 --> 00:42:35,376
No!

725
00:42:35,520 --> 00:42:36,886
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

726
00:42:39,257 --> 00:42:40,850
Miss me? (LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

727
00:42:42,360 --> 00:42:43,919
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

728
00:42:47,098 --> 00:42:48,259
GORDON: Open it, let's go.

729
00:42:51,769 --> 00:42:53,203
GUARD: Sound the alarm!

730
00:42:53,704 --> 00:42:55,263
(ALARM RINGING)

731
00:43:44,489 --> 00:43:45,548
English-US-Template
